{"files": [{"id": 42161530, "name": "pgen.1010903.g001.tif", "size": 965936, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/42161530", "supplied_md5": "42fa80d60b60d077927e10d2d4336221", "computed_md5": "42fa80d60b60d077927e10d2d4336221", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 842833, "full_name": "Karine Normandin", "first_name": "Karine", "last_name": "Normandin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 126532, "full_name": "Jasmin Coulombe-Huntington", "first_name": "Jasmin", "last_name": "Coulombe-Huntington", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892359, "full_name": "Corinne St-Denis", "first_name": "Corinne", "last_name": "St-Denis", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892362, "full_name": "Alexandre Bernard", "first_name": "Alexandre", "last_name": "Bernard", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9592382, "full_name": "Mohammed Bourouh", "first_name": "Mohammed", "last_name": "Bourouh", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 470436, "full_name": "Thierry Bertomeu", "first_name": "Thierry", "last_name": "Bertomeu", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1118, "full_name": "Mike Tyers", "first_name": "Mike", "last_name": "Tyers", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Mike_Tyers", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 73964, "full_name": "Vincent Archambault", "first_name": "Vincent", "last_name": "Archambault", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Vincent_Archambault", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/A_chemogenomic_screen_identifies_enhancers_and_suppressors_of_partial_PLK1_inhibition_/24044770", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p><b>A.</b> Screen design. A NALM-6 clonal cell line allowing doxycycline-inducible Cas9 expression was transduced with the EKO sgRNA library. After blasticidin selection for the presence of sgRNA constructs, doxycycline was added and cells were allowed to proliferate for 8 days with or without the compounds as indicated. Cells were then harvested and submitted to Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) to quantify the relative amounts of each sgRNA constructs in the different cell populations. <b>B.</b> Pairwise comparisons of gene RANKS scores obtained in the 3 screens with the different PLK1 inhibitors. Negative scores indicate enhancers and positive scores indicate suppressors. Names of selected hit genes of interest are labeled. <b>C.</b> Results distribution showing average RANKS score and combined P-value across the 3 screens for each gene. Names of selected hit genes of interest are labeled. <b>D.</b> Protein interaction network of genes identified as enhancers and suppressors of partial PLK1 inhibition in the screens. Interactions (lines) are those reported in BioGRID or IntACT. Only genes with False Discovery Rates (FDR) < 0.001 were included. Colors indicate selected representative enriched GO terms. FDR-corrected P-values for selected GO terms are: 6.0 X 10<sup>\u221222</sup> for Chromosomes, Centromeric region; 2.6 X 10<sup>\u221217</sup> for Kinetochore; 9.0 X 10<sup>\u22126</sup> for Microtubule-organizing center; 7.4 X 10<sup>\u22128</sup> for Cell cycle process; 5.0 X 10<sup>\u22125</sup> for Regulation of cell cycle (these last 2 terms were grouped into Cell cycle in the figure). <b>E.</b> Distribution of RANKS scores for <i>KIF18A</i> and <i>SKA1</i> in 399 screens with 303 bioactive compounds. The top 3 screens with the most extreme scores are indicated. Note that they were conducted with the 3 PLK1 inhibitors tested. Coordinate values used to generate graphs in panels B-C and E are available in <a href=\"http://www.plosgenetics.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903#pgen.1010903.s018\" target=\"_blank\">S2 Table</a> and <a href=\"http://www.plosgenetics.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903#pgen.1010903.s017\" target=\"_blank\">S1</a> Data, respectively.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 965936, "created_date": "2023-08-28T17:33:59Z", "modified_date": "2023-09-08T18:01:48Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["xlink \"> polo", "wide screening strategy", "threonine kinase required", "spindle assembly checkpoint", "like kinase 1", "cell division cycle", "compromised cells resulted", "nuclear reassembly defects", "different kinetochore perturbations", "rendering cells hypersensitive", "partial plk1 inactivation", "partial plk1 inhibition", "partial inhibition", "cancer cells", "often hypersensitive", "mitotic defects", "kinetochore complex", "plk1 compromises", "plk1 activity", "results suggest", "promising target", "notably factors", "multiple ways", "genetic enhancers", "functionally linked", "extremely sensitive", "dependent cenp", "crucially depend", "completely effective", "combinatorial therapies", "clinical trials", "chemical inhibitors", "based genome", "also show"], "keywords": ["xlink \"> polo", "wide screening strategy", "threonine kinase required", "spindle assembly checkpoint", "like kinase 1", "cell division cycle", "compromised cells resulted", "nuclear reassembly defects", "different kinetochore perturbations", "rendering cells hypersensitive", "partial plk1 inactivation", "partial plk1 inhibition", "partial inhibition", "cancer cells", "often hypersensitive", "mitotic defects", "kinetochore complex", "plk1 compromises", "plk1 activity", "results suggest", "promising target", "notably factors", "multiple ways", "genetic enhancers", "functionally linked", "extremely sensitive", "dependent cenp", "crucially depend", "completely effective", "combinatorial therapies", "clinical trials", "chemical inhibitors", "based genome", "also show"], "categories": [{"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 12, "title": "Cell Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 14, "title": "Molecular Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 19, "title": "Pharmacology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 873, "title": "Chemical Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 734, "title": "Biological Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 61, "title": "Developmental Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 64, "title": "Cancer", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 128, "title": "Hematology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Normandin, Karine; Coulombe-Huntington, Jasmin; St-Denis, Corinne; Bernard, Alexandre; Bourouh, Mohammed; Bertomeu, Thierry; et al. (2023). A chemogenomic screen identifies enhancers and suppressors of partial PLK1 inhibition.. PLOS Genetics. Figure. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903.g001", "related_materials": [{"id": 147166354, "identifier": "10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903", "title": "Genetic enhancers of partial PLK1 inhibition reveal hypersensitivity to kinetochore perturbations", "relation": "IsSupplementTo", "identifier_type": "DOI", "is_linkout": true, "link": "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903"}], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "i